IMPORT prelude

-- Allied Health Professions Act 2011 (Singapore) -- which professions the Act regulates (ss 2, 4, First and Second Schedules), who is
-- "duly qualified" (s 3), temporary registration periods (s 19), appeals against refusal and removal (ss 21(7), 26(3), 55(1)),
-- practising certificates (s 23), the title offences and who else they catch (ss 29 to 34), the Part 4 penalty (s 36), what a
-- Disciplinary Tribunal or a voluntary request may lead to (ss 37(1)(d), 53(2)), and composition (s 73).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition (incorporating amendments up to 1 December 2021, in operation 31 December 2021), informal
-- consolidation, version in force from 5 December 2025, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/AHPA2011.txt. The latest
-- amendment annotated in the deposit is Act 19 of 2025 (Statutes (Miscellaneous Amendments) Act 2025), wef 5 December 2025.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0020 in ../../../requirements.jsonl: Tier 2 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by everyday-life
-- relevance. It asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has asked a sharper question yet.
-- SCOPED to what a patient, a practitioner, a student or an employing clinic meets. Not encoded: the Council and its committees
-- (Part 2), the registers and the full/restricted/conditional eligibility tests beyond their outcome (ss 14 to 18), the complaints,
-- mediation, investigation, Health Committee and Interim Orders procedure (Part 5 Divisions 2 to 4, 6 to 8), the Third Column
-- descriptions of each profession's acts, regulations made under s 75, and the s 76 transitional deeming.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Allied Health Professions Act 2011 -- practice`

§§ `2, 4, First and Second Schedules -- which professions the Act regulates`

-- s 2: "allied health professional" means a person with a qualification "in any of the allied health professions listed in the First
-- Schedule"; "prescribed allied health profession" means one "set out in the first column of the Second Schedule".
-- s 4: "This Act applies only in relation to allied health professions set out in the Second Schedule."
-- First Schedule (ten, listed by the professional's name): Audiologist, Clinical Psychologist, Dietitian, Occupational Therapist,
-- Physiotherapist, Podiatrist, Prosthetist/Orthotist, Radiation Therapist, Radiographer, Speech Therapist.
-- Second Schedule, first column (five): Occupational Therapy, Physiotherapy, Speech-Language Pathology, Radiation Therapy,
-- Radiography. (The enum below names each discipline; mapping "Speech Therapist" to Speech-Language Pathology is by name.)
DECLARE Profession IS ONE OF
    audiology
    `clinical psychology`
    dietetics
    `occupational therapy`
    physiotherapy
    podiatry
    `prosthetics and orthotics`
    `radiation therapy`
    radiography
    `speech therapy`

GIVEN `the profession` IS A Profession
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Act applies to` IF
    CONSIDER `the profession`
    WHEN `occupational therapy` THEN TRUE
    WHEN physiotherapy THEN TRUE
    WHEN `speech therapy` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `radiation therapy` THEN TRUE
    WHEN radiography THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- Second Schedule, second column (titles): Occupational Therapist, Ergotherapist; Physiotherapist, Physical Therapist; six speech
-- titles including Speech Therapist and Speech Pathologist; Radiation Therapist, Therapeutic Radiographer; Diagnostic Radiographer,
-- Radiographer, Radiologic Technologist. The last four titles below name First Schedule professions with no Second Schedule entry.
DECLARE Title IS ONE OF
    `Occupational Therapist`
    `Ergotherapist`
    `Physiotherapist`
    `Physical Therapist`
    `Speech Therapist`
    `Speech Pathologist`
    `Radiation Therapist`
    `Therapeutic Radiographer`
    `Diagnostic Radiographer`
    `Radiographer`
    `Radiologic Technologist`
    `Dietitian`
    `Clinical Psychologist`
    `Podiatrist`
    `Audiologist`

GIVEN `the title` IS A Title
GIVETH A Profession
`the profession named by` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the title`
    WHEN `Occupational Therapist` THEN `occupational therapy`
    WHEN `Ergotherapist` THEN `occupational therapy`
    WHEN `Physiotherapist` THEN physiotherapy
    WHEN `Physical Therapist` THEN physiotherapy
    WHEN `Speech Therapist` THEN `speech therapy`
    WHEN `Speech Pathologist` THEN `speech therapy`
    WHEN `Radiation Therapist` THEN `radiation therapy`
    WHEN `Therapeutic Radiographer` THEN `radiation therapy`
    WHEN `Diagnostic Radiographer` THEN radiography
    WHEN `Radiographer` THEN radiography
    WHEN `Radiologic Technologist` THEN radiography
    WHEN `Dietitian` THEN dietetics
    WHEN `Clinical Psychologist` THEN `clinical psychology`
    WHEN `Podiatrist` THEN podiatry
    WHEN `Audiologist` THEN audiology

-- A title is reserved when it names a profession the Act applies to (s 29(1)(c) reaches the second-column titles, "or any other word
-- in any language having the same meaning"; foreign-language equivalents are not modelled).
GIVEN `the title` IS A Title
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the title is reserved` IF
    `the Act applies to` (`the profession named by` `the title`)

§§ `3 -- duly qualified allied health professional`

-- s 3: "duly qualified allied health professional" means "a person who is a registered allied health professional AND has a valid
-- practising certificate". Registration alone is not enough.
GIVEN `is registered` IS A BOOLEAN, `holds a valid practising certificate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is duly qualified` IF
    `is registered` AND `holds a valid practising certificate`

§§ `19(3) -- temporary registration periods`

-- s 19(3): temporary registration "is for a period not exceeding 2 years which may be renewed ... for a further period or periods
-- each not exceeding 12 months".
GIVEN `is a renewal` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the longest temporary registration in months` MEANS
    IF `is a renewal` THEN 12 ELSE 24

§§ `21(7), 26(3), 55(1) -- where an appeal lies and how long there is`

-- s 21(7): a refusal to register -- "within 30 days of the notice ... appeal to the Minister whose decision is final".
-- s 26(3): a removal order by the Council (failed conditions, fraud, withdrawn qualification, foreign deregistration) -- "within
-- 30 days of being notified of the order, appeal to the Minister whose decision is final".
-- s 55(1): an order of a Disciplinary Tribunal -- "within 30 days after the notice of the order is served", appeal to the General
-- Division of the High Court.
DECLARE Decision IS ONE OF
    `a refusal to register`
    `a removal from the register by the Council`
    `a Disciplinary Tribunal order`

DECLARE Forum IS ONE OF
    `the Minister`
    `the General Division of the High Court`

GIVEN `the decision` IS A Decision
GIVETH A Forum
`the appeal lies to` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the decision`
    WHEN `a Disciplinary Tribunal order` THEN `the General Division of the High Court`
    OTHERWISE `the Minister`

GIVEN `the decision` IS A Decision
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the appeal decision is final` IF
    `the appeal lies to` `the decision` EQUALS `the Minister`

GIVEN `days after notice` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the appeal is in time` IF
    `days after notice` AT MOST 30

§§ `23 -- practising certificates`

-- s 23(4): renewal "must be made no later than 30 days before the expiry"; (5): one who applies "later than 30 days before the
-- expiry ... shall be liable to pay ... such late application fee as may be prescribed".
GIVEN `days before expiry` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a late application fee is payable` IF
    `days before expiry` LESS THAN 30

-- s 23(8), (9): on suspension or cancellation, or lapse, removal or suspension of registration (when the certificate "is deemed to be
-- cancelled"), the certificate must be surrendered "within 14 days". (10): failure -- "a fine not exceeding $5,000".
GIVEN `surrendered` IS A BOOLEAN, `days taken` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `failing to surrender is an offence` IF
    (NOT `surrendered`) OR `days taken` GREATER THAN 14

`the maximum fine for failing to surrender` MEANS 5000

§§ `29, 30 -- false assumption of title`

-- s 29(1): a person who is NOT duly qualified commits an offence if he or she (a) "wilfully and falsely pretends" to be duly
-- qualified; (b) practises under the style or title of an allied health professional; (c) "takes or uses any name or title set out
-- in the second column of the Second Schedule"; (d) uses any "name, title, sign, uniform, badge" implying qualification; or (e)
-- advertises or holds himself or herself out as one.
-- (2): (d) "does not apply" to acts in training under the supervision of a registered professional in an approved establishment.
-- (3): defence to (c), (d) or (e) -- "to prove that the person acted without the intention to deceive or to gain any advantage,
-- benefit or financial gain" for a business, trade, profession, vocation or employment. (4): no (3) defence to (e) "in the
-- prescribed circumstances".
DECLARE Conduct IS ONE OF
    `wilfully pretending to be duly qualified`
    `practising under the title of the profession`
    `using a Second Schedule title`
    `using a uniform or badge implying qualification`
    `advertising as an allied health professional`

GIVEN `the conduct` IS A Conduct, `in supervised training at an approved establishment` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `proved no intent to deceive or gain` IS A BOOLEAN, `in prescribed circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the conduct is an offence under section 29` IF
    CONSIDER `the conduct`
    WHEN `wilfully pretending to be duly qualified` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `practising under the title of the profession` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `using a Second Schedule title` THEN NOT `proved no intent to deceive or gain`
    WHEN `using a uniform or badge implying qualification` THEN
        (NOT `in supervised training at an approved establishment`) AND (NOT `proved no intent to deceive or gain`)
    WHEN `advertising as an allied health professional` THEN
        `in prescribed circumstances` OR (NOT `proved no intent to deceive or gain`)

-- Using a title, ss 29(1)(c) and 30(1)(c) together: a person not duly qualified may use no reserved title (s 29); a duly qualified
-- person may use only the titles of "the authorised profession", the one "for which he or she is registered and issued a practising
-- certificate" (s 30). The s 29(3) / 30(3) defence applies to both.
GIVEN `the title` IS A Title, `is registered` IS A BOOLEAN, `holds a valid practising certificate` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the authorised profession` IS A Profession, `proved no intent to deceive or gain` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `using the title is an offence` IF
        `the title is reserved` `the title`
    AND (NOT (`is duly qualified` `is registered` `holds a valid practising certificate`
              AND `the profession named by` `the title` EQUALS `the authorised profession`))
    AND (NOT `proved no intent to deceive or gain`)

§§ `31(3), (4), 33, 34 -- employers, enablers and suspended persons`

-- s 31(3): where an offence under s 29 or 30 is committed by a person acting as "an employee, an agent or a partner" of another, the
-- other "shall also be guilty of an offence". (4): defence -- to prove the offence was committed "without B's knowledge AND" that B
-- "has taken all reasonable precautions and exercised due diligence".
GIVEN `the employee committed a title offence` IS A BOOLEAN, `proved it was without the employer's knowledge` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `proved all reasonable precautions and due diligence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the employer is also guilty` IF
        `the employee committed a title offence`
    AND (NOT (`proved it was without the employer's knowledge` AND `proved all reasonable precautions and due diligence`))

-- s 33(1): a registered professional who "has knowingly enabled a person, whether described as an assistant or otherwise, to assume
-- a title in contravention of section 29 or 30". (2): defence of mistake, reliance or cause beyond control AND all reasonable
-- precautions and due diligence.
GIVEN `knowingly enabled an assistant to assume a title` IS A BOOLEAN, `proved mistake or cause beyond control` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `proved reasonable precautions` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the enabling professional is guilty` IF
        `knowingly enabled an assistant to assume a title`
    AND (NOT (`proved mistake or cause beyond control` AND `proved reasonable precautions`))

-- s 34: a person suspended under Part 5 "must not practise in ANY prescribed allied health profession during the period of
-- suspension" -- not only the profession of registration.
GIVEN `suspended under Part 5` IS A BOOLEAN, `practised a prescribed profession during the suspension` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the suspended person commits an offence` IF
    `suspended under Part 5` AND `practised a prescribed profession during the suspension`

§§ `36 -- general penalty for Part 4`

-- s 36: "a fine not exceeding $25,000 or ... imprisonment for a term not exceeding 6 months or ... both and, in the case of a second
-- or subsequent conviction, ... $50,000 or ... 12 months or ... both".
GIVEN `is a repeat conviction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum Part 4 fine` MEANS
    IF `is a repeat conviction` THEN 50000 ELSE 25000

GIVEN `is a repeat conviction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum Part 4 imprisonment in months` MEANS
    IF `is a repeat conviction` THEN 12 ELSE 6

§§ `37(1)(d), 53(2) -- suspension and penalty`

-- s 53(2)(b): a Disciplinary Tribunal may suspend registration "for a period of at least 3 months and not more than 3 years";
-- (e) impose "a penalty not exceeding $50,000".
-- s 37(1)(d): a professional who believes his or her fitness is impaired may request suspension "for a period of not more than
-- 3 years" -- with no minimum.
GIVEN `months` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Tribunal may suspend for` IF
    `months` AT LEAST 3 AND `months` AT MOST 36

GIVEN `amount` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Tribunal may impose a penalty of` IF
    `amount` AT MOST 50000

GIVEN `months` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a voluntary suspension may be requested for` IF
    `months` GREATER THAN 0 AND `months` AT MOST 36

§§ `73 -- composition`

-- s 73(1): the Council may compound an offence "prescribed as a compoundable offence" for "a sum not exceeding the lower of" (a) "one
-- half of the amount of the maximum fine that is prescribed for the offence" and (b) "$2,000". Which offences are prescribed was not
-- read (regulations not deposited).
GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lower of` MEANS
    IF `a` AT MOST `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

GIVEN `maximum fine` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the most a composition can be` MEANS
    `the lower of` (`maximum fine` DIVIDED BY 2) 2000
